  "investigation_notes": "Upload failure investigated \u2014 `10/12` checks used.\n\n**Root cause: inode exhaustion on `/srv/lab-data` filesystem**\n\n* `E4`: `/srv/lab-data` `mountpoint=/srv/lab-data`, `use_percent=37.3` with `available_mb=282.9` but `inode_use_percent=100.0` \u2014 blocks free, inodes exhausted.\n* `E5`: `incidentlab-app-1` `running=true`, `mount source=/srv/lab-data destination=/data rw=true`, `user=1000:1000`, `oom_killed=false`, `exit_code=0` \u2014 container running, mount writable, not OOM.\n* `E7`: app logs show symptom:\n  * `POST /upload 500` with `OSError: [Errno 28] No space left on device: '/data/tmp/...part' at File \"/app/main.py\", line 55, in upload`\n  * `GET /health 503` with `OSError: [Errno 28] No space left on device: '/data/uploads/.health-...' at File \"/app/main.py\", line 116, in health` + `health check failed`\n* `E2`: `http://localhost:8080/health status_code=503 body=unhealthy` \u2014 matches `E7` health failure, so `503` is symptom not separate cause.\n\n**Ruled out:**\n\n* Permissions: `E9` `/srv/lab-data/uploads is_dir=true owner 1000:1000 mode 0755 app_uid 1000 app_user_can_write=true`.\n* Database dependency: `E6` `incidentlab-db-1 status=running health=healthy` + `E8` `database system is ready to accept connections` + `E1` both `state=running`.\n* Root filesystem full: `E10` `path=/ mountpoint=/ use_percent=6.8 inode_use_percent=1.5`.\n* Crash/restart loop as cause: `E1` `Up 21s / Up 26s` + `E3` single `kill/stop/die/destroy/rename` at `2026-10-28T23:48:05` then `start` + `health_status: healthy` for db \u2014 recent recreate, now stable running.\n* Block-capacity full on data volume: `E4` `used_mb=168.5 available_mb=282.9 use_percent=37.3`.\n\n`Errno 28` with free blocks (`E4`) + `100%` inodes (`E4`) explains write failures to `/data/tmp` and `/data/uploads` (`E7`) despite writable mount (`E5`) and permissions (`E9`).\n",
